    {
      "week": "Week 44",
      "title": "A face turned into the window",
      "ratio": "4:5",
      "credit": "Behrouz Sasani",
      "creditURL": "https://www.pexels.com",
      "cover": "pick-window-portrait",
      "points": [
        "Turn the face into the glass, not away from it: the lit cheek and the shadowed jaw make the portrait.",
        "Expose for the skin, then let the window frame blow to white so the light comes from inside the picture.",
        "Leave the shoulder and one hand in frame — a portrait needs a body, not just a head, to read at print size."
      ],
