    {
      "week": "Week 45",
      "title": "Where the water draws the line",
      "ratio": "3:4",
      "credit": "Red Zeppelin",
      "creditURL": "https://www.pexels.com",
      "cover": "pick-shoreline",
      "points": [
        "Shoot straight down and keep the foam line level across the frame; a tilted horizon ruins the abstraction.",
        "Include one tiny figure on the sand so the bands of water, wet sand and dry sand keep their scale.",
        "Keep the dark wet band under a third of the height, otherwise the print reads as a grey stripe."
